 "about_text": "OXY ARTS is the public arts center of Occidental College, located on York Boulevard in the Highland Park area of Los Angeles. It presents free exhibitions, performances, artist residencies (including the Wanlass Artist-in-Residence program), and workshops spanning film, visual art, performance, writing, and music. The program emphasizes projects led by Black, Indigenous, and people-of-color artists and organizers, and work that engages social and political issues. It also serves as a gateway to Occidental College's arts departments, offering hands-on internship and teaching opportunities for students, especially BIPOC and first-generation students, while building relationships with the wider Los Angeles arts community.",
